%I A398184 #62 Sep 14 2026 18:42:59
%S A398184 1,1,23,347,5646,116411,2445518,66509584
%N A398184 Number of maximal subsets of the n X n grid with no three collinear points (subsets to which no further grid point can be added without creating a collinear triple).
%C A398184 These are the facets of the independence complex of the collinear-triples hypergraph of the n X n grid (A398172 counts all its faces). Their sizes range from A277433(n) (Martin Gardner's minimum no-3-in-a-line problem, all slopes) to 2n; exactly A000755(n) of them have the maximum size 2n. The complex is not pure for n >= 3.
%C A398184 Subsets are counted as sets of grid points; rotations and reflections are counted separately, as in A000755.
%H A398184 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="/A398184/a398184.txt">Numbers of maximal subsets by size, n = 1..7</a>
%e A398184 For n = 3 there are 23 maximal subsets: 5 of size 4, 16 of size 5 and 2 of size 6 (the two 6-point no-three-in-line solutions of the 3 X 3 grid).
%o A398184 (Python) # See links in A398172.
%Y A398184 Cf. A398172 (all subsets), A398580 (all subsets by size), A000755, A000769, A000938, A277433.
%K A398184 nonn,more,new
